    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0649" n="553" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg553"/>

                <head>No. 321.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Sir Edward Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 24,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 6th instant,
                    in which you request to be informed as to what extent the right of
                    transportation of goods and passengers is granted to Canadian vessels plying
                    between ports of the United States, where such transportation is not regulated
                    by articles XXVI, XXVII, or XXX of the treaty of Washington, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith, for your information, a copy of a letter of the 11th instant,
                    upon the subject, from the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d323-a1.xml" xpointer="d323-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
